			"text": "Axelrodichthys was a lobe-finned fish discovered in Africa, Europe, South America and Possibly North America; dating back to Cretaceous. It was named in honour of the American ichthyologist 'Herbert R. Axelrod' with the combination of the Greek word 'fish'. It was a big fish, growing to 1-2 meters long. The species that lived during the Early Cretaceous inhabited brackish waters while the Late Cretaceous species were fresh water exclusive."
